# OneThought Infrastructure - Cursor AI Rules

## 🔗 Project Architecture (TWO REPOSITORIES)

This is **ONE OF TWO connected repositories**:

| Repository | Purpose | Location |
|------------|---------|----------|
| **OneThought** | Next.js application code | `/Users/kaz1mir/Documents/OneThought` |
| **onethought-infra** (THIS) | AWS/Kubernetes infrastructure | `/Users/kaz1mir/Documents/onethought-infra` |

### How They Connect:
```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                     OneThought (App)                            │
│  - Next.js 14 application                                       │
│  - React components, API routes                                 │
│  - Supabase client integration                                  │
│  - Dockerfile in root for container builds                      │
│  GitHub: Kaz1miR-nevo/onepost                                   │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              │ Docker image pushed to ECR
                              │ Helm deploys to EKS
                              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│              onethought-infra (THIS REPOSITORY)                 │
│  - Terraform: AWS EKS, VPC, ECR, WAF                           │
│  - Helm: Kubernetes deployments                                 │
│  - values.stage.yaml / values.prod.yaml                        │
│  - Monitoring: Grafana, Loki, Prometheus                       │
│  GitHub: Kaz1miR-nevo/onethought-infra                         │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
                              │
                              ▼
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                      Supabase (Database)                        │
│  Stage: cgiqlvscetphwvvffdlj.supabase.co                       │
│  Prod:  hutrzgxhgnkkkvwmlytm.supabase.co                       │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

### When to Work in Each Repo:

**Work in OneThought (app) when:**
- Adding/modifying React components
- Creating API routes
- Changing database schema (migrations)
- Fixing bugs in application code
- Running local development

**Work HERE (onethought-infra) when:**
- Changing Kubernetes resources (replicas, memory, CPU)
- Modifying AWS infrastructure (VPC, EKS, IAM)
- Updating Helm values (environment variables, secrets)
- Setting up monitoring/alerts
- Deploying to stage/prod clusters
- Scaling, networking, security configurations

